  "summary_en": "This is the UK government's March 2023 white paper (Command Paper 815). It proposes a pro-innovation, context-based framework for regulating AI. Five cross-sector principles would be applied by existing sector regulators rather than through new AI legislation. Central government functions for risk monitoring, M&E and coordination would support them, along with an AI regulatory sandbox and work on international interoperability.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Five principles: safety, security and robustness; transparency and explainability; fairness; accountability and governance; contestability and redress",
   "Principles initially non-statutory, implemented by existing regulators with possible future statutory duty",
   "Central functions for risk assessment, monitoring and evaluation, and regulatory coordination",
   "Establish a multi-regulator AI sandbox per Vallance recommendation",
   "Regulate use context rather than specific technologies; promote standards and international interoperability"
  ],
